# JavaScript Quick Reference

## Pattern
```javascript
// ✅ Arrow function IIFE
(() => {
	const element = document.querySelector('.element');
	if (!element) return;

	element.addEventListener('click', handleClick);
})();
```

## Formatting
```javascript
// NO spaces in parentheses (standard JS, not PHP style)
if (condition) { }
document.querySelector('.selector');
functionName(arg1, arg2);

// Tabs for indentation
// camelCase naming
const headerNavToggle = document.querySelector('.header-nav-toggle');
```

## Variables
```javascript
const element = document.querySelector('.element'); // Default
let counter = 0;                                    // Only if reassigning
// Never use var
```

## DOM Pattern
```javascript
(() => {
	// Cache elements
	const element = document.querySelector('.element');

	// Early return
	if (!element) return;

	// Event handlers
	const handleClick = (event) => {
		event.preventDefault();
		element.classList.toggle('js-active');
	};

	// Bind events
	element.addEventListener('click', handleClick);
})();
```

## Class Toggling
```javascript
const activeClass = 'js-active';

element.classList.add(activeClass);
element.classList.remove(activeClass);
element.classList.toggle(activeClass);
element.classList.contains(activeClass);
```

## Async/Await
```javascript
const fetchData = async (url) => {
	try {
		const response = await fetch(url);
		if (!response.ok) throw new Error('HTTP error');
		return await response.json();
	} catch (error) {
		console.error('Error:', error);
		return null;
	}
};
```
